# Run the application first with `docker compose up --build` (default URL: http://localhost:8000).
# This file uses the VS Code REST Client response-variable syntax.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness (also checks the database)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Create a short link
# @name createLink
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "target_url": "https://example.com/docs",
  "expires_in_seconds": 3600
}

### Follow the new link (a successful redirect increments click_count)
GET {{baseUrl}}/r/{{createLink.response.body.code}}

### Read aggregate statistics after the redirect
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/links/{{createLink.response.body.code}}/stats

### Optional custom alias
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "target_url": "https://example.com/interview",
  "custom_alias": "interview-demo"
}

### Validation error example (expected: 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "target_url": "javascript:alert(1)"
}

### Missing-link example (expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/r/does-not-exist
